---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Factory-farmed chickens" description="Visualizing the number of factory-farmed chickens alive in the United States at any given moment" ogImage="/og/page/factory-farmed-chickens.png?v=2">

  <article class="chickens-viz">
    <h1>Factory-farmed chickens</h1>

    <div class="prose intro-text">
      <p>At any given moment, approximately <strong>1.6 billion chickens</strong> are alive in <a href="https://www.newrootsinstitute.org/articles/what-is-chicken-factory-farming-and-how-bad-is-it">factory farm conditions</a> in the United States — about 1.2 billion broilers raised for meat and 400 million hens kept for eggs.</p>

      <p>If you packed those 1.2 billion meat chickens together at typical factory-farm density, they would fill roughly <a href="https://royalsocietypublishing.org/doi/10.1098/rsos.210478"><strong>32 square miles</strong></a> — a patch of land smaller than many cities. That's about 58,000 birds per acre, or <strong>115 times</strong> as dense as the <a href="https://www.freedomrangerhatchery.com/blog/square-feet-per-chicken/">suggested humane standard of 500 per acre</a>.</p>

      <p>It's impossible to hold a number like 1.6 billion in your head. Below are 1.6 billion dots, one for each chicken. Scroll down to see them all. For more info on the life of a chicken represented by each dot <a href="https://www.newrootsinstitute.org/articles/what-is-chicken-factory-farming-and-how-bad-is-it">you can read this page</a>. <a href="https://stories.theplotline.org/cafo-explorer/map/#5.45/33.686/-84.1">This is a map of where chicken farms are distributed in a few states</a>.</p>

      <p>If you would like to help end this, the single best thing you can do is set up a recurring donation to an effective animal charity. <a href="https://www.farmkind.giving/compassion-calculator">This website</a> is one among many with recommendations for where to donate, and has estimates of how many animals you can save.</p>

      <figure>
        <img
          src="/images/broiler-house.jpg"
          alt="White broiler chickens packed shoulder to shoulder across the litter floor of a commercial chicken house, around a line of red pan feeders"
          width="1600"
          height="1063"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>Broilers in a commercial chicken house in Luling, Texas. Photo: <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/usdagov/54673505087/">USDA</a>, public domain.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <!-- The scale ladder: the field's own dots at the field's own size, so a
         reader can count before they can't. Canvases are drawn by the same
         code as the field; the numbers are filled in for this screen. -->
    <div class="prose scale-ladder" id="scale-ladder">
      <div class="scale-ladder__figure">
        <canvas id="ladder-one" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        <span class="scale-ladder__label">One chicken</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scale-ladder__figure">
        <canvas id="ladder-hundred" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        <span class="scale-ladder__label">100 chickens</span>
      </div>
      <p class="scale-ladder__note">Each screenful of dots below is about <span id="ladder-screen">11,000</span> chickens. A million chickens is about <span id="ladder-million">90</span> screenfuls. All 1.6 billion is about <span id="ladder-all">150,000</span>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="viz-wrapper" id="viz-wrapper">
      <div class="viz-counter viz-counter--hidden" id="viz-counter">
        <span class="viz-counter-pct" id="viz-pct">0.00%</span>
        <span class="viz-counter-num" id="viz-num">0 / 1,600,000,000</span>
      </div>
      <div class="viz-scroll-area" id="viz-scroll-area">
        <canvas id="viz-canvas"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose outro-text">
      <p><a href="https://www.farmkind.giving/compassion-calculator">Consider donating to an effective animal charity</a></p>
    </div>

  </article>

</Base>

<style>
  .chickens-viz h1 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .intro-text {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .outro-text {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .scale-ladder {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .scale-ladder__figure + .scale-ladder__figure {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .scale-ladder__figure canvas {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Same apparatus as a figcaption: small, dim, left-aligned. */
  .scale-ladder__label {
    display: block;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-note);
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .scale-ladder__note {
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0;
  }

  .viz-wrapper {
    margin-left: calc(-50vw + 50%);
    width: 100vw;
  }

  .viz-scroll-area {
    position: relative;
    max-width: calc(var(--max-width) * 2);
    margin: 0 auto;
    /* height set by JS */
  }

  #viz-canvas {
    display: block;
    position: sticky;
    /* top set by JS to sit below counter */
  }

  .viz-counter {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 10;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 10px 24px;
    max-width: calc(var(--max-width) * 2);
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: var(--bg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    transition: background 0.3s, opacity 0.4s ease;
  }

  .viz-counter--hidden {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .viz-counter-pct {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
    min-width: 5em;
  }

  .viz-counter-num {
    font-size: var(--font-size-small);
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .chickens-viz h1 {
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }

    .viz-counter {
      padding: 8px 16px;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .viz-counter-pct {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initChickensViz);

  function initChickensViz() {
    const canvas = document.getElementById('viz-canvas') as HTMLCanvasElement;
    const scrollArea = document.getElementById('viz-scroll-area');
    const wrapper = document.getElementById('viz-wrapper');
    const counter = document.getElementById('viz-counter');
    const pctEl = document.getElementById('viz-pct');
    const numEl = document.getElementById('viz-num');
    if (!canvas || !scrollArea || !wrapper || !counter || !pctEl || !numEl) return;

    if ((wrapper as any).__vizInit) return;
    (wrapper as any).__vizInit = true;

    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    if (!ctx) return;

    const TOTAL_DOTS = 1_600_000_000;
    // Rows are composed from short pre-rendered segments (SEG cells each),
    // picked per row and position from SEG_VARIANTS tiles. See prerender().
    const SEG = 16;
    const SEG_VARIANTS = 32;
    const ladderOne = document.getElementById('ladder-one') as HTMLCanvasElement | null;
    const ladderHundred = document.getElementById('ladder-hundred') as HTMLCanvasElement | null;

    // Everything that depends on the viewport lives here and is recomputed
    // by layout(): on load, and again whenever the window is resized or
    // zoomed (a phone's address bar collapsing counts). Before this the
    // canvas was sized once, so a taller window left a blank band under
    // the dots.
    let dpr = 1;
    let screenWidth = 0;
    let counterHeight = 0;
    let viewHeight = 0;
    let isMobile = false;
    let CELL = 10;
    let DOT_RADIUS = 3;
    let cols = 0;
    let totalRows = 0;
    let virtualHeight = 0;
    let scrollScale = 1;
    let segCanvases: HTMLCanvasElement[] = [];
    let lastScrollY = -1;

    // mulberry32: a tiny seeded PRNG, so the jitter is the same every time.
    function seededRandom(seed: number): () => number {
      let a = seed >>> 0;
      return () => {
        a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;
        let t = a;
        t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);
        t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);
        return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;
      };
    }

    // One dot per cell, nudged by up to 15% of the cell and sized within
    // +/-10% of the nominal radius. Extremes stay inside the cell, so rows
    // never clip.
    function drawDotGrid(g: CanvasRenderingContext2D, columns: number, rows: number, seed: number) {
      const rand = seededRandom(seed);
      g.beginPath();
      for (let row = 0; row < rows; row++) {
        for (let col = 0; col < columns; col++) {
          const cx = col * CELL + CELL / 2 + (rand() - 0.5) * 0.3 * CELL;
          const cy = row * CELL + CELL / 2 + (rand() - 0.5) * 0.3 * CELL;
          const r = DOT_RADIUS * (0.9 + rand() * 0.2);
          g.moveTo(cx + r, cy);
          g.arc(cx, cy, r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        }
      }
      g.fill();
    }

    function getDotColor(): string {
      const theme = document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-theme');
      return theme === 'dark' ? '#e8e6e1' : '#1a1918';
    }

    // Pre-render short segments of a row (SEG cells wide, one cell tall)
    // into offscreen canvases. Then render() composes each visible row from
    // them — far faster than drawing thousands of arcs each frame.
    //
    // Segments rather than whole rows, and many of them: a single tile made
    // every row identical, so a wheel step that moved a whole number of rows
    // left the field looking frozen; eight whole-row variants fixed that but
    // repeated often enough that the eye caught the same row going by. With
    // 32 segment variants chosen per (row, position), two rows match only if
    // all their segments do, which at eight segments a row never happens.
    // Each segment nudges every dot a little (position and size, seeded so
    // it is stable across re-renders); dots stay inside their cells, so
    // segments butt together without seams.
    function prerender() {
      const color = getDotColor();
      segCanvases.forEach((c, v) => {
        const g = c.getContext('2d')!;
        g.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
        g.clearRect(0, 0, SEG * CELL, CELL);
        g.fillStyle = color;
        drawDotGrid(g, SEG, 1, 1000 + v);
      });
    }

    // Which variant a segment uses: a cheap 2D integer hash of (row,
    // position), so neighbours differ and the choice is stable for a given
    // spot — the field never shimmers between frames.
    function segmentVariant(row: number, seg: number): number {
      let h = Math.imul(row + 1, 0x9e3779b1) ^ Math.imul(seg + 1, 0x85ebca6b);
      h ^= h >>> 15;
      h = Math.imul(h, 0x2c1b3c6d);
      h ^= h >>> 12;
      return (h >>> 0) % SEG_VARIANTS;
    }

    // The scale ladder above the field: one dot and a 10x10 block, drawn
    // with the same cells, dots, and jitter as the field, so they are a
    // literal sample of it.
    function drawLadder() {
      const color = getDotColor();
      const draw = (c: HTMLCanvasElement | null, n: number, seed: number) => {
        if (!c) return;
        const size = n * CELL;
        c.width = size * dpr;
        c.height = size * dpr;
        c.style.width = size + 'px';
        c.style.height = size + 'px';
        const g = c.getContext('2d')!;
        g.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
        g.fillStyle = color;
        drawDotGrid(g, n, n, seed);
      };
      draw(ladderOne, 1, 1);
      draw(ladderHundred, 10, 100);
    }

    // The ladder note's numbers, filled in for this screen: dots per
    // screenful of the field, and how many screenfuls a million and 1.6
    // billion come to.
    function fillLadderNumbers() {
      const rowsPerScreen = Math.max(1, Math.floor(viewHeight / CELL));
      const dotsPerScreen = cols * rowsPerScreen;
      const roundTo = (n: number, step: number) => Math.round(n / step) * step;
      const fill = (id: string, text: string) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el) el.textContent = text;
      };
      fill('ladder-screen', roundTo(dotsPerScreen, 100).toLocaleString());
      fill('ladder-million', Math.round(1_000_000 / dotsPerScreen).toLocaleString());
      fill('ladder-all', roundTo(TOTAL_DOTS / dotsPerScreen, 1000).toLocaleString());
    }

    function layout() {
      dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
      screenWidth = scrollArea!.clientWidth;
      counterHeight = counter!.offsetHeight;
      viewHeight = Math.max(1, window.innerHeight - counterHeight);

      // Cell size. The spacer below is capped and scroll is scaled to cover
      // the whole virtual height, so this sets only how big each dot reads,
      // never how far the page scrolls: every dot is unmistakably a dot, and
      // the scale comes from the counter and the ladder above the field.
      // (Earlier versions derived a 3-6px cell from a virtual page height,
      // which read as texture rather than as dots.)
      isMobile = window.innerWidth < 768;
      CELL = isMobile ? 8 : 10;
      DOT_RADIUS = CELL * 0.3;
      cols = Math.max(1, Math.floor(screenWidth / CELL));
      totalRows = Math.ceil(TOTAL_DOTS / cols);
      virtualHeight = totalRows * CELL;

      // Cap spacer height to stay within browser limits. The spacer is the
      // whole scroll track, so a longer one means a slower pass through the
      // dots: 24M px is about 0.5 rows per scrolled pixel on desktop (it was
      // 15M, about 0.8). Chromium and WebKit lay out to ~33.5M px; Gecko
      // stops at ~17.9M and clamps anything taller, so read the height back
      // and scale to whatever the browser actually gave us. Mobile browsers
      // crash at very tall elements, so use a much lower cap there.
      const MAX_SAFE = isMobile ? 5_000_000 : 24_000_000;
      const requestedHeight = Math.min(virtualHeight, MAX_SAFE);
      scrollArea!.style.height = requestedHeight + 'px';
      const actualHeight = Math.floor(scrollArea!.getBoundingClientRect().height);
      const spacerHeight = actualHeight > 0 && actualHeight < requestedHeight
        ? actualHeight
        : requestedHeight;
      scrollScale = virtualHeight / spacerHeight;

      // Canvas: viewport-sized, sticky below counter
      canvas.width = screenWidth * dpr;
      canvas.height = viewHeight * dpr;
      canvas.style.width = screenWidth + 'px';
      canvas.style.height = viewHeight + 'px';
      canvas.style.top = counterHeight + 'px';
      ctx!.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);

      segCanvases = [];
      for (let v = 0; v < SEG_VARIANTS; v++) {
        const c = document.createElement('canvas');
        c.width = Math.ceil(SEG * CELL * dpr);
        c.height = Math.ceil(CELL * dpr);
        segCanvases.push(c);
      }
      prerender();
      drawLadder();
      fillLadderNumbers();
      lastScrollY = -1;
    }

    function render() {
      const scrollAreaRect = scrollArea!.getBoundingClientRect();
      const rawScrollY = -(scrollAreaRect.top);

      const roundedScroll = Math.round(rawScrollY);
      if (roundedScroll === lastScrollY) return;
      lastScrollY = roundedScroll;

      const virtualScrollY = rawScrollY * scrollScale;
      const clampedY = Math.max(0, Math.min(virtualScrollY, virtualHeight - viewHeight));

      const rowStart = Math.floor(clampedY / CELL);
      const rowEnd = Math.min(Math.ceil((clampedY + viewHeight) / CELL), totalRows);

      ctx!.clearRect(0, 0, screenWidth, viewHeight);

      const segs = Math.ceil(cols / SEG);
      for (let row = rowStart; row < rowEnd; row++) {
        const y = row * CELL - clampedY;
        // Compose this row from pre-rendered segments at this y position.
        // The last segment is cut to the columns that remain, so no dot is
        // drawn past the count the counter is keeping.
        for (let seg = 0; seg < segs; seg++) {
          const tile = segCanvases[segmentVariant(row, seg)];
          const cells = Math.min(SEG, cols - seg * SEG);
          ctx!.drawImage(
            tile,
            0, 0, cells * CELL * dpr, tile.height,
            seg * SEG * CELL, y, cells * CELL, CELL
          );
        }
      }

      // Update counter — count dots scrolled past (top of viewport)
      const rowsScrolledPast = Math.floor(clampedY / CELL);
      const dotsScrolledPast = Math.min(TOTAL_DOTS, rowsScrolledPast * cols);
      const fraction = dotsScrolledPast / TOTAL_DOTS;
      pctEl!.textContent = (fraction * 100).toFixed(2) + '%';
      numEl!.textContent = dotsScrolledPast.toLocaleString() + ' / 1,600,000,000';

      // Fade in counter once user starts scrolling
      if (dotsScrolledPast > 0) {
        counter!.classList.remove('viz-counter--hidden');
      } else {
        counter!.classList.add('viz-counter--hidden');
      }
    }

    layout();

    // Theme change: re-render the row stamps and the ladder, force a redraw
    const themeObserver = new MutationObserver(() => {
      prerender();
      drawLadder();
      lastScrollY = -1;
      render();
    });
    themeObserver.observe(document.documentElement, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['data-theme']
    });

    // Scroll handler with rAF throttle
    let ticking = false;
    function onScroll() {
      if (!ticking) {
        requestAnimationFrame(() => {
          render();
          ticking = false;
        });
        ticking = true;
      }
    }
    window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });

    // Resize or zoom: re-lay out once things settle. The counter only
    // depends on scroll position and spacer height, so the count a reader
    // is looking at does not jump when the field re-flows.
    let resizeTimer = 0;
    function onResize() {
      window.clearTimeout(resizeTimer);
      resizeTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
        layout();
        render();
      }, 150);
    }
    window.addEventListener('resize', onResize);

    // Cleanup on Astro navigation
    document.addEventListener('astro:before-swap', () => {
      window.removeEventListener('scroll', onScroll);
      window.removeEventListener('resize', onResize);
      window.clearTimeout(resizeTimer);
      themeObserver.disconnect();
    }, { once: true });

    // Initial render
    render();
  }
</script>
